{"type":"message","id":"8a8304bf","parentId":"006f0ab0","timestamp":"2026-07-15T13:05:41.650Z","message":{"role":"user","content":"SYSTEM ARCHITECT DIRECTIVE: EVALUATE ROADMAP & AGENT DEPLOYMENT\nTARGET: Jnr's Local Execution Plan\n\nJnr, we have achieved a 100% green health check baseline on Base 1. Excellent work.\n\nBefore we write more code, we want your developer evaluation on how to proceed. We have three main paths, but we need to balance \"tying up loose ends\" with building future capabilities. \n\nProvide your direct feedback on the following:\n\n1. IDENTIFY THE LOOSE ENDS:\n   Look at our current directory (C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\). What pending files, unapproved skills (like Tess's validator), or raw configurations still need to be cleaned up or locked down to make our current footprint 100% stable?\n\n2. THE RESEARCH CRON JOB:\n   We want to set up a lightweight, local background task (a cron job or Windows Task Scheduler script) that periodically runs a research agent. This agent's sole job is to search for and summarize new AI/Ollama developments that we can use to optimize the WASP system.\n   - How should we structure this script on Base 1?\n   - What local model/API should it query?\n   - How should it output its research to us without causing background CPU bloat?\n\nGive us your direct architectural recommendation. What should we execute next to keep this system running optimally all the time?","timestamp":1784120738631,"idempotencyKey":"cc2d5b8f-9e0d-45da-90fd-ac622848fb6c:user"}}
