   7/15/2026   2:14 PM              4 .gitignore                                                           \r\n-a----         7/15/2026   2:58 PM           2476 base1_status.ps1                                                     \r\n-a----         7/15/2026   1:22 AM           1951 outbound_queue.json                                                  \r\n-a----         7/15/2026   1:22 AM           3799 outreach_engine.js                                                   \r\n-a----         7/15/2026   1:22 AM            182 sourced_leads.json","cwd":"C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784120811402}}
{"type":"message","id":"43c508d2","parentId":"4a46c1f2","timestamp":"2026-07-15T13:07:11.131Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Loose‑ends in `C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\`**\n\n| File / Item | Status | Recommended Action |\n|-------------|--------|--------------------|\n| `.env` | Live copy of template – **OK** | Keep; ensure it remains `.gitignore`‑ed. |\n| `.env.template** | Reference – **OK** | Keep as‑is. |\n| `.gitignore** | Contains `.env` – **OK** | No change needed. |\n| `base1_status.ps1` | Health‑check script – **100 % green** | Keep; it is now stable. |\n| `wasp-payload-validator` skill proposal | **Pending** (ID `wasp-payload-validator-20260715-0c5b1f5c35`) | Review and **approve** (`skill_workshop action=apply …`) or explicitly reject if not needed. |\n| `outbound_queue.json`, `outreach_engine.js`, `sourced_leads.json** | Appear to be test/scratch files from earlier work. | If they are no longer used, **delete** or move to an archive folder (`archive/`) to keep the workspace clean. |\n| Any other stray `.log`, `.tmp`, `.bak` files | None visible | Run a quick `Get-ChildItem -File -Exclude .ps1,.json,.js,.env,.template,.gitignore` to confirm; delete anything unnecessary. |\n\n**Next step to lock down the footprint:**  \nApprove the validator skill (or remove the proposal) and purge/archive the three JSON/JS files. After that, the directory will contain only the essential, version‑controlled assets.\n\n---\n\n### Research‑Cron Recommendation (lightweight, local‑first)\n\n**Goal:** Periodically poll for new AI/Ollama developments, summarize them with a local model, and deposit a short briefing where you can see it without adding CPU load.\n\n#### 1. Where to store the output\nCreate a dedicated log/file:  \n`C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\research_brief.md`  \nEach run will append a timestamped section.\n\n#### 2. What the script does (PowerShell – ~30 lines)\n```powershell\n# research_ollama.ps1\n# Place this script in the Chief Madithi folder.\n# It queries a public, low‑volume source (e.g., Hugging Face blog RSS or arXiv query)\n# then uses the local Ollama/qwen2.5 model to produce a 3‑sentence summary.\n\n$logPath = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'research_brief.md'\n$timestamp = Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'\n\n# --- 1. Pull a candidate feed (example: Hugging Face blog RSS) ---\ntry {\n    $rss = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'https://huggingface.co/blog/rss.xml' -TimeoutSec 10\n    # Take the most recent entry (<item>)\n    $item = $rss.rss.channel.item[0]\n    $title = $item.title\n    $link  = $item.link\n    # Grab a snippet – first 500 chars of description\n    $snippet = ($item.description -replace '<[^>]+>', '').TrimEnd().Substring(0,500)\n} catch {\n    Write-Warning \"Feed fetch failed: $_\"\n    exit 1\n}\n\n# --- 2. Ask local Ollama to summarize ---\n$prompt = @\"\nSummarize the following AI/Ollama‑related news in exactly three sentences, suitable for a technical executive briefing:\n\nTitle: $title\nSnippet: $snippet\n\nSummary:\n\"@\n\n# Call Ollama via its REST API (default localhost:11434)\ntry {\n    $ollamaResponse = Invoke-RestMethod `\n        -Uri 'http://localhost:127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate' `\n        -Method Post `\n        -Body (@{\n            model  = 'qwen2.5'          # or whatever local model you have loaded\n            prompt = $prompt\n            stream = $false\n        } | ConvertTo-Json) `\n        -ContentType 'application/json' `\n        -TimeoutSec 15\n\n    $summary = $ollamaResponse.response.Trim()\n} catch {\n    Write-Warning \"Ollama call failed: $_\"\n    $summary = \"[Ollama summary unavailable]\"\n}\n\n# --- 3. Append to the briefing file ---\n$entry = @\"\n### $timestamp\n**Source:** $title ($link)\n\n$summary\n\n\"@\nAdd-Content -Path $logPath -Value $entry\n\n# Optional: keep only last 20 entries to bound file size\n$lines = Get-Content $logPath\nif ($lines.Count -gt 200) {   # ~20 entries * ~10 lines each\n    $lines[-200..-1] | Set-Content $logPath\n}\n```\n\n**Why this design?**\n- **Local model only:** Uses the already‑running Ollama/qwen2.5 instance; no extra GPU/CPU spikes beyond normal inference.\n- **Low‑bandwidth source:** RSS feed is lightweight and can be swapped (e.g., arXiv API query for `ollama` or `LLM`).\n- **Bound output:** The script truncates the log file, preventing uncontrolled growth.\n- **Non‑intrusive:** Can be scheduled to run every 4‑6 hours; each run finishes in < 10 seconds on a modest CPU.\n\n#### 3. Hook it into OpenClaw cron (recommended)\nUse the built‑in cron tool so the job appears in the gateway’s schedule and you get automatic failure alerts if desired.\n\n```bash\n# Add a cron job (run from any OpenClaw session)\ncron add `\n  --name \"wasp-research-ollama\" `\n  --schedule \"0 */4 * * *\" `   # every 4 hours, at minute 0\n  --payload '{\n      \"kind\":\"agentTurn\",\n      \"message\":\"& { powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\MikeT\\\\Projects\\\\Chief Madithi\\\\research_ollama.ps1\\\" }\",\n      \"timeoutSeconds\":30\n  } `\n  --sessionTarget current `\n  --target current   # deliver output as a systemEvent to the main session\n  --delivery.mode announce   # you’ll see the result in chat\n  --delivery.bestEffort $true\n```\n\n- The `message` runs the PowerShell script in a isolated agentTurn (so it doesn’t block your main session).  \n- If you prefer a simple file‑only approach, drop `--sessionTarget current` and let the script write to `research_brief.md`; you can view it whenever you like.\n\n#### 4. Expected outcome\n- Every 4 hours you’ll get a fresh, three‑sentence briefing appended to `research_brief.md` (or announced in chat).  \n- No persistent background daemon; the job is started, runs, and exits.  \n- If Ollama is down, the script logs a clear warning and still creates an entry (so you know the attempt happened).  \n\n**Actionable next steps for you (as Monty):**\n\n1. **Approve or discard** the pending `wasp-payload-validator` skill.  \n2. **Clean up** the three test files (`outbound_queue.json`, `outreach_engine.js`, `sourced_leads.json`) – delete or move to an `archive/` subfolder.  \n3. **Create** the `research_ollama.ps1` script (copy the block above) in the Chief Madithi folder.  \n4. **Add** the cron job via the `cron add` command shown (adjust frequency if you prefer a different cadence).  \n5. **Validate** by manually running the script once (`.\\research_ollama.ps1`) and checking that `research_brief.md` receives a new entry.\n\nOnce those are done, the workspace will be in a 100 % stable state with a low‑overhead, self‑feeding research loop running automatically. Let me know if you’d like me to execute any of those steps directly."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784120811425,"responseId":"chatcmpl-51d5dd23-1e5d-4a6e-b1a3-56205fcd6d42"}}
