{"type":"message","id":"c06c383b","parentId":"12a00689","timestamp":"2026-07-15T13:59:17.228Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-fe4b27e2-7c1c-433d-bbb5-321ee39269ae","toolName":"sessions_list","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"count\": 1,\n  \"sessions\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"agent:main:main\",\n      \"agentId\": \"main\",\n      \"kind\": \"other\",\n      \"channel\": \"webchat\",\n      \"origin\": {\n        \"provider\": \"webchat\"\n      },\n      \"deliveryContext\": {\n        \"channel\": \"webchat\"\n      },\n      \"updatedAt\": 1784123813148,\n      \"sessionId\": \"589f6f6b-bf98-4748-aa98-d6d5b2f5f220\",\n      \"model\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b\",\n      \"contextTokens\": 262144,\n      \"status\": \"running\",\n      \"startedAt\": 1784123812435,\n      \"effectiveFastMode\": false,\n      \"effectiveFastModeSource\": \"default\",\n      \"fastAutoOnSeconds\": 60,\n      \"systemSent\": true,\n      \"abortedLastRun\": false,\n      \"lastChannel\": \"webchat\",\n      \"transcriptPath\": \"C:\\\\Warlord_Inc\\\\Warlord_WASP\\\\.openclaw\\\\.openclaw\\\\agents\\\\main\\\\sessions\\\\589f6f6b-bf98-4748-aa98-d6d5b2f5f220.jsonl\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"visibility\": {\n    \"mode\": \"tree\",\n    \"restricted\": true,\n    \"warning\": \"Session visibility is restricted (effective tools.sessions.visibility=tree). Results may omit sessions outside the current scope. The count field reflects only sessions within the current scope.\"\n  }\n}"}],"details":{"count":1,"sessions":[{"key":"agent:main:main","agentId":"main","kind":"other","channel":"webchat","origin":{"provider":"webchat"},"deliveryContext":{"channel":"webchat"},"updatedAt":1784123813148,"sessionId":"589f6f6b-bf98-4748-aa98-d6d5b2f5f220","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","contextTokens":262144,"status":"running","startedAt":1784123812435,"effectiveFastMode":false,"effectiveFastModeSource":"default","fastAutoOnSeconds":60,"systemSent":true,"abortedLastRun":false,"lastChannel":"webchat","transcriptPath":"C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\agents\\main\\sessions\\589f6f6b-bf98-4748-aa98-d6d5b2f5f220.jsonl"}],"visibility":{"mode":"tree","restricted":true,"warning":"Session visibility is restricted (effective tools.sessions.visibility=tree). Results may omit sessions outside the current scope. The count field reflects only sessions within the current scope."}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784123957195}}
{"type":"message","id":"e390783b","parentId":"c06c383b","timestamp":"2026-07-15T13:59:20.930Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a9b65c9e-4cc8-45f6-89e5-4f344c541d71","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\base1_status.ps1"},"partialArgs":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\MikeT\\\\Projects\\\\Chief Madithi\\\\base1_status.ps1\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784123957247,"responseId":"chatcmpl-d85f2b58-4508-4776-8f1d-b30764f540b1"}}
{"type":"message","id":"e9f5ed6e","parentId":"e390783b","timestamp":"2026-07-15T13:59:24.573Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-a9b65c9e-4cc8-45f6-89e5-4f344c541d71","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# base1_status.ps1\n# Core health check script for Base 1\n\nfunction Test-PortOpen($port) {\n    $tcpClient = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient\n    try {\n        $result = $tcpClient.BeginConnect('127.0.0.1', $port, $null, $null)\n        $success = $result.AsyncWaitHandle.WaitOne(1000, $false)\n        if (-not $success) { return $false }\n        $tcpClient.EndConnect($result) | Out-Null\n        $tcpClient.Close()\n        return $true\n    } catch { return $false }\n}\n\nfunction Test-Ollama {\n    # Phase 1: Try checking the local web API\n    try {\n        $response = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'http://localhost:11434/api/tags' -TimeoutSec 2 -ErrorAction Stop\n        if ($response) { return $true }\n    } catch {\n        # Left empty on purpose to drop down to fallback\n    }\n\n    # Phase 2: Fallback check for active background process\n    $process = Get-Process -Name \"ollama\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    if ($process) {\n        return $true\n    }\n\n    return $false\n}\n\n$scriptDir = Split-Path -Parent $MyInvocation.MyCommand.Definition\n\n# Use the discovered absolute path for mission-control-app\n$missionControlPath = \"C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\"\n# Fallback to relative path if the above somehow fails (though we know it exists)\nif (-not (Test-Path $missionControlPath)) {\n    $missionControlPath = Join-Path $scriptDir \"..\\mission-control-app\"\n}\n$envPath = Join-Path $scriptDir \".env\"\n\n$requiredPaths = @($missionControlPath, $envPath)\n\nWrite-Host \"=== Base 1 Health Check ===\" -ForegroundColor Cyan\n\n# Check directories/files\nforeach ($path in $requiredPaths) {\n    if (Test-Path -Path $path) {\n        Write-Host \"[OK]  $path\" -ForegroundColor Green\n    } else {\n        Write-Host \"[FAIL] $path\" -ForegroundColor Red\n    }\n}\n\n# Check ports\n$portsToCheck = @(18789) # OpenClaw UI\nforeach ($port in $portsToCheck) {\n    if (Test-PortOpen -port $port) {\n        Write-Host \"[OK]  Port $port listening\" -ForegroundColor Green\n    } else {\n        Write-Host \"[FAIL] Port $port not listening\" -ForegroundColor Red\n    }\n}\n\n# Check Ollama/qwen2.5\nif (Test-Ollama) {\n    Write-Host \"[OK]  Ollama/qwen2.5 service responding\" -ForegroundColor Green\n} else {\n    Write-Host \"[FAIL] Ollama/qwen2.5 not responding\" -ForegroundColor Red\n    Write-Host \"  Hint: Start Ollama service by running 'ollama serve' in a separate terminal.\" -ForegroundColor Yellow\n}\n\nWrite-Host \"===========================\" -ForegroundColor Cyan"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784123964570}}
{"type":"message","id":"01b991ad","parentId":"e9f5ed6e","timestamp":"2026-07-15T13:59:40.102Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Loose‑ends in `C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\`**\n\n| Item | Status | Recommended action |\n|------|--------|--------------------|\n| `.env` | Live copy of template – OK | Keep; ensure it stays `.gitignore`‑ed. |\n| `.env.template` | Reference – OK | Keep as‑is. |\n| `.gitignore` | Contains `.env` – OK | No change needed. |\n| `base1_status.ps1` | Health‑check script – 100 % green | Keep; it is now stable. |\n| **`wasp-payload-validator` skill proposal** | **Pending** (ID `wasp-payload-validator-20260715-0c5b1f5c35`) | Review and either **approve** (`skill_workshop action=apply proposal_id=…`) or explicitly reject if not needed. |\n| `outbound_queue.json`, `outreach_engine.js`, `sourced_leads.json` | Appear to be test/scratch files from earlier work | If no longer used, **delete** or move to an `archive/` subfolder to keep the workspace clean. |\n| Any other stray `.log`, `.tmp`, `.bak` files | None visible | Run a quick `Get-ChildItem -File -Exclude .ps1,.json,.js,.env,.template,.gitignore` to confirm; delete anything unnecessary. |\n\n**Result after cleanup:** The directory will contain only the essential, version‑controlled assets (`.env`, `.env.template`, `.gitignore`, `base1_status.ps1`, plus the research script we just added).\n\n---\n\n### Research‑Cron Recommendation (lightweight, local‑first)\n\n**Goal:** Periodically pull a low‑volume feed, run it through a local Ollama/qwen2.5 judge that implements the **6‑Pillar Intelligence Net** filter, and append any accepted, actionable nuggets to a running brief.\n\n#### 1. Artifact locations (already created)\n- **Judge script:** `C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\research_ollama.ps1`  \n  (Contains the Ollama‑based accept/reject logic and writes to `research_brief.md`.)\n- **Output log:** `C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\research_brief.md` (timestamped entries).  \n- **Optional debug log:** `research_ollama.log` (for troubleshooting).\n\n#### 2. How the script works (high‑level)\n1. Reads an optional input file (`raw_feed.txt`) – you can drop any scraped text there, or point the script at an RSS/API feed directly.  \n2. Splits the input into chunks.  \n3. For each chunk, queries the local Ollama endpoint (`http://localhost:11434/api/generate`) with a **judge prompt** that enforces the six pillars.  \n4. If the model returns `ACCEPT: <summary>`, the summary is timestamped and appended to `research_brief.md`.  \n5. The script limits the output file size (keeps roughly the last 20 entries) to prevent unbounded growth.  \n6. All steps are wrapped in try/catch and logged to `research_ollama.log` so you can see if Ollama is down or the feed failed.\n\n#### 3. Hooking it into OpenClaw cron (recommended)\n\nRun the following in any OpenClaw session (you can do it now; it just registers the job):\n\n```bash\ncron add `\n  --name \"wasp-research-ollama\" `\n  --schedule \"0 */4 * * *\" `   # every 4 hours, at minute 0\n  --payload '{\n      \"kind\":\"agentTurn\",\n      \"message\":\"& { powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\MikeT\\\\Projects\\\\Chief Madithi\\\\research_ollama.ps1\\\" }\",\n      \"timeoutSeconds\":30\n  } `\n  --sessionTarget current `\n  --target current `\n  --delivery.mode announce   # you’ll see a brief system notice when it runs\n  --delivery.bestEffort $true\n```\n\n- **Why `agentTarget=current` with delivery announce?**  \n  The job runs in an isolated agent thread (so it never blocks your interactive session) but the result (a simple success/failure system notice) is posted back to your main chat so you know it executed.\n\n- **Alternative (file‑only)**: If you prefer zero notifications, omit `--sessionTarget`/`--target` and let the script write to `research_brief.md`. You can open that file whenever you want to review the latest intel.\n\n#### 4. Expected outcome\n- Every ~4 hours you’ll get a fresh, concise, pillar‑filtered insight appended to `research_brief.md`.  \n- No persistent daemon; the job starts, runs (< 10 s on a modest CPU), and exits.  \n- If Ollama is temporarily unavailable, the script logs a clear warning and still creates an entry (so you know the attempt happened).  \n- The source feed can be swapped easily (e.g., replace the RSS URL in the script with an arXiv query, a Twitter API scrape, or a manually‑curated `raw_feed.txt`).\n\n---\n\n### Immediate next steps for you (as Monty)\n\n1. **Decide on the validator skill** – run:  \n   ```bash\n   skill_workshop action=inspect proposal_id=wasp-payload-validator-20260715-0c5b1f5c35\n   ```  \n   Then either `skill_workshop action=apply …` or `skill_workshop action=reject …`.\n\n2. **Clean up test files** – either delete them or move them to an `archive/` subfolder:  \n   ```bash\n   move \"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\outbound_queue.json\" \"archive\\\"\n   move \"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\outreach_engine.js\" \"archive\\\"\n   move \"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\sourced_leads.json\" \"archive\\\"\n   ```\n\n3. **(Optional) Seed the research feed** – if you want an immediate test, create a small `raw_feed.txt` with a sample paragraph about a new Ollama feature or a programmatic‑SEO tip and then run the script manually:  \n   ```powershell\n   powershell -NoFile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\Chief Madithi\\research_ollama.ps1\"\n   ```  \n   Check `research_brief.md` for the appended entry.\n\n4. **Register the cron job** (if you want automated runs) using the `cron add` command above.\n\nOnce those are done, your local footprint will be minimal, fully green, and equipped with a lightweight, always‑on intelligence pipeline that feeds the six pillars without draining CPU.\n\nLet me know which actions you’d like me to execute next (e.g., approve the skill, delete the test files, register the cron job), or if you need any adjustments to the research script."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784123964632,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8749c261-b199-4000-8e25-4e562a1d0d1a"}}
