{"type":"message","id":"5021f5eb","parentId":"ba00ec8b","timestamp":"2026-07-15T14:19:09.312Z","message":{"role":"user","content":"==================================================================\nPROJECT EXECUTION DIRECTIVE: FIRST LIVE RUN\nPROJECT NAME: WASP Core Update Project\n==================================================================\n\nJnr, no more preparation. We are officially live on \"WASP Core Update Project.\" \n\nWe need to execute our very first active research run right now to verify the 6-Pillar filtering logic works end-to-end. \n\nComplete these three tasks immediately:\n\n1. INITIALIZE THE PROJECT DIRECTORY:\n   - Create the directory: \"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\\"\n   - Move \"base1_status.ps1\", \"research_ollama.ps1\", and your new \"wasp_org_structure.json\" into this clean project folder so the old \"Chief Madithi\" folder has zero active script pollution.\n   - Update your desktop shortcut (\"Base 1 Health Check.lnk\") to point to the new location of \"base1_status.ps1\".\n\n2. SEED THE FEED:\n   - Create a text file: \"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\raw_feed.txt\"\n   - Paste the following raw intelligence snippet into that file for the judge to analyze:\n     \"Alex Finn's Mission Control update (March 2026) reveals the ultimate local Next.js framework for OpenClaw. It integrates a live Kanban task board tracking autonomous sub-agents, a sidebar activity feed for heartbeat checks, and a visual 2D pixel-art office representing running local models. It uses local file paths instead of complex cloud databases to keep user data 100% secure and offline on the local network.\"\n\n3. EXECUTE THE PIPELINE:\n   - Run your \"research_ollama.ps1\" script manually in the new project directory.\n   - Verify that your local \"qwen2.5\" model on port 11434 successfully judges the snippet, accepts it under the \"UI & Control Dashboards\" pillar, and generates our first executive summary.\n\nConfirm when the files are successfully relocated, the script has run, and paste the exact contents of \"C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\research_brief.md\" here for Mike and Monty to review!","timestamp":1784125146455,"idempotencyKey":"789ebc39-a99e-4c18-aff5-ec738bc1101d:user"}}
